/P 47 0 R
/E (Figure 8. JAF Racing Team project timeline. Each bar runs from the start of a stage to the start of the next one; the diamonds mark the first official test \(September 30\) and the final car submission \(October 5\).)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (We also used the Gantt chart to help with the division of responsibilities. Each member could identify the tasks they were responsible for and understand how their work contributed to the overall project. This helped us avoid confusion, distribute the workload more effectively, and make sure that important tasks were not forgotten. As the project progressed, we could also review what had already been completed and identify what still needed attention.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [35]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Another important benefit was that the Gantt chart helped us manage our time and stay organized. Since our project included several areas such as engineering, design, testing, documentation, marketing, and presentation, having everything organized in one timeline gave us a clearer view of the whole process. When changes or delays occurred, we could adjust our tasks and reorganize our priorities instead of losing track of the overall schedule.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [36]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (Overall, the Gantt chart helped us turn our project into a structured and manageable process. It gave us a clear timeline, helped us divide responsibilities, coordinate our work, monitor our progress, and make sure that each stage of the JAF Racing Team project was completed before moving on to the next one. It was an important part of keeping the team organized and working toward the same final goal.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [37]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The Gantt chart allowed us to clearly see the timeline and progression of our project. We divided larger objectives into smaller tasks and placed them according to the dates when they needed to be completed. This made it easier to understand which tasks were a priority and which ones depended on previous work being finished. It also helped us coordinate the different areas of the team because some tasks had to be completed before others could begin. For example, the initial design had to be developed before we could produce and test physical components, and the testing results had to be reviewed before making further improvements to the car.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [38]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (A Gantt chart is a project management tool that helps organize the different tasks of a project by showing what needs to be done, when it needs to be done, and how long each task will take. We used a Gantt chart to plan and divide the work of the JAF Racing Team throughout the entire project. Instead of completing tasks without a clear order, we organized our work into different stages, starting with the first school visit and team organization and continuing through the car design, construction, testing, improvements, marketing, and final submission.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [39]
>>
endobj
